Tue Oct 27 10:37:06 UTC 2026 - Tina Müller <timueller+perl@suse.de>

- updated to 1.240.0 (1.24)
   see /usr/share/doc/packages/perl-HTTP-Body/Changes

  1.24      2026-10-26 18:28:01+01:00 Europe/Berlin
  	- SECURITY, CVE-2026-116131: urlencoded bodies are limited to
  	  $HTTP::Body::UrlEncoded::max_params fields and multipart bodies to
  	  $HTTP::Body::MultiPart::max_parts parts (1000 each); reported and
  	  patched by CPANSec. bsc#1288644
  	- SECURITY, CVE-2026-116132: the temporary file of an upload that is
  	  still incomplete at DESTROY-time is now always deleted; reported and
  	  patched by CPANSec (also fixes RT#84004) bsc#1288645
  	- SECURITY, CVE-2026-116133: a multipart body without a boundary or with
  	  a malformed delimiter line no longer takes quadratic time; a malformed
  	  delimiter line now croaks, and padding or an epilogue after the close
  	  delimiter is accepted; reported and patched by CPANSec. bsc#1288646
  	- SECURITY, CVE-2026-116134: a multipart part's header block is limited
  	  to $HTTP::Body::MultiPart::max_header_size bytes (32768) and
  	  $HTTP::Body::MultiPart::max_header_lines lines (100); reported and
  	  patched by CPANSec. bsc#1288647
  	- SECURITY, CVE-2026-116135: mixed-case percent escapes (e.g. %aB) in
  	  urlencoded bodies are decoded instead of being dropped; reported and
  	  patched by CPANSec. bsc#1288648
  	- SECURITY, CVE-2026-116285: the chunk size line of a chunked body is
  	  matched in linear instead of quadratic time bsc#1288649
  	- SECURITY, CVE-2026-116531: a chunked body is now framed independently
  	  of where the reads feeding add() fall; a read that split a chunk could
  	  leave the parser never reaching 'done', hanging a server that reads
  	  until done bsc#1288650
  	- INCOMPATIBLE: add() now croaks when one of the new limits is exceeded.
  	  Raise the variable, or set it to 0 to disable that limit, if your
  	  forms need more. See NOTES in HTTP::Body.
  	- RT#105021: temp-file write errors in MultiPart and OctetStream now
  	  croak instead of silently truncating the stored body
  	- RT#123615: a NUL byte in a multipart filename is stripped so it cannot
  	  truncate a path handed on downstream
  	- Moved repository from Shadowcat git to GitHub (libwww-perl/HTTP-Body)
  	- Updated all metadata resources to point to GitHub
  	- Fixed prerequisites: moved Digest::MD5 to test deps, changed HTTP::Headers to HTTP::Message
  	- Added README.md for GitHub
  	- Updated support section in documentation
  	- Moved the POD, POD coverage and Perl::Critic tests to xt/release, so
  	  they run on every release instead of being skipped

